    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `bulkSignupWarning` flag on the owner response.\n\n**What the spec needed:** when more than 80 owners have already been created \"today\" (i.e. share the relevant registration date, excluding the owner itself), the response should carry `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`. The acceptance test reads the field back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, so it had to be present on every owner response, not just the create path.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean (readOnly) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 this is where the existing derived response fields already live (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipTier`, `locality`), so it's the natural home. Converted the mapper from an interface to an abstract class (the project uses `defaultComponentModel=spring`, so it's a Spring bean) and injected `ClinicService`. Added a `bulkSignupWarning(owner)` helper mapped via expression that counts owners sharing the owner's `registrationDate`, excluding the owner itself, and returns `true` when that count exceeds 80.\n\n**Design notes:**\n- Excluding the owner by id means that on a create the count reflects the owners that *already* existed that day (mirroring the `> 80 already created` wording), and it stays consistent when the same owner is later fetched via GET.\n- This reuses the same per-day accumulation the existing daily-limit rule enforces against (`DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT = 100`), so the warning at 80 fires before the hard reject at 100, and the flag is uniform across the create, single-GET, and list/page responses.\n- Returns `false` for owners with no registration date; no dependency cycle since `ClinicService` doesn't depend on any mapper.",
